# The byte-preservation acceptance criterion of milestone 0.1a is: open every
# fixture, save it unchanged, and `git status --porcelain` must be empty. That
# test is only meaningful if git stores and checks out these files byte for
# byte — line-ending normalisation would rewrite the very bytes under test and
# turn a passing run into evidence of nothing.
#
# `-text` disables all EOL conversion and keeps the working tree identical to
# the blob on every platform, Windows CI included.
fixtures/** -text

# Keep diffs of the corpus out of review noise; they are generated data.
fixtures/** linguist-generated=true
